  "body": "This one is a little different than other aliases, because AFAIK no browser has shipped unprefixed yet &mdash; so this will have to be defined as an alias to a different vendor-prefixed property.\n\nHere's the draft spec: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-size-adjust/#text-size-adjust\n\nMicrosoft implements this as an alias for `-ms-text-size-adjust`: https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/dn793579%28v=vs.85%29.aspx\n\n> As of Internet Explorer for Windows Phone 8.1 Update, Internet Explorer for Windows Phone supports \"-webkit-text-size-adjust\" as an alias for this property. \n\nGecko implements this an as alias for `-moz-text-size-adjust`: https://dxr.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/source/layout/style/test/property_database.js#6535\n\n(Given the amount of unprefixed `text-size-adjust` on the web (following all the prefixed declarations), I'd be surprised if the unprefixed spec version tried to change semantics: cf., https://github.com/search?l=css&p=7&q=text-size-adjust&ref=simplesearch&type=Code&utf8=%E2%9C%93).\n",
